# Local-only development defaults.
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored). Do not use these values in production.
#
# Compose interpolates this file for docker-compose.yml.
# `go run ./cmd/api` loads it via internal/config so both share the same URLs.

# HTTP bind for the control-plane API (loopback, not 0.0.0.0).
FORGE_API_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8080

# Phase 3: the first operator is created via POST /auth/bootstrap (dashboard
# /login) when the users table is empty. Do not put a password here.

# Postgres role created by the official image on first boot.
FORGE_POSTGRES_USER=forge
FORGE_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=forge
FORGE_POSTGRES_DB=forge

# Host port mapped to container 5432. 15432 avoids a common Windows clash
# with a native Postgres already bound to 5432.
FORGE_POSTGRES_HOST_PORT=15432

# The API talks to Postgres on the *host* port (15432), not 5432 inside
# the container. sslmode=disable is local-only.
FORGE_DATABASE_URL=postgres://forge:forge@127.0.0.1:15432/forge?sslmode=disable

FORGE_REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0

# Worker → Caddy admin (Compose publishes 2019 on loopback only).
FORGE_CADDY_ADMIN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:2019
FORGE_CADDY_UPSTREAM_HOST=host.docker.internal
FORGE_PROXY_PUBLIC_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:9080

# Phase 7.6 custom domains: Caddy ACME (HTTP-01 / TLS-ALPN-01) needs
# :80 and :443 reachable at the hostname. Compose still publishes
# 127.0.0.1:9080/9443. Map 80:80 and 443:443 yourself to issue certs.
# Never publish Caddy admin (:2019).

# Phase 5 — optional API TLS (both or neither). Generate with:
#   go run ./cmd/forge-cert
# FORGE_TLS_CERT_FILE=.forge/tls/cert.pem
# FORGE_TLS_KEY_FILE=.forge/tls/key.pem

# Env-at-rest key. Empty = create/read .forge/data.key. API and worker
# must share it. Never commit the file or paste the hex into chat.
# FORGE_DATA_KEY=
# FORGE_DATA_KEY_FILE=.forge/data.key

# Quotas (defaults shown). Disk cap is on the fetched workspace, not the container.
# FORGE_MAX_PROJECTS_PER_OWNER=20
# FORGE_MAX_INFLIGHT_DEPLOYS=2
# FORGE_MAX_INFLIGHT_PER_NODE=4
# FORGE_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS=14
# FORGE_WORKSPACE_MAX_BYTES=268435456

# Phase 6 — second worker on this machine or a lab VM. Default name is local
# (no token). A named node needs POST /nodes then FORGE_NODE_TOKEN once.
# FORGE_NODE_NAME=local
# FORGE_NODE_TOKEN=
# FORGE_NODE_ADVERTISE_HOST=

# Required to bind 0.0.0.0. Auth is still required. The API refuses to start
# unless TLS cert and key are set and FORGE_DATABASE_URL does not use the
# password "forge". Keep Caddy admin on 127.0.0.1:2019. This flag is not
# an AWS deploy.
# FORGE_ALLOW_PUBLIC_BIND=

# Phase 7.7 GitHub OAuth (both or neither). Register an OAuth App with
# callback http://127.0.0.1:3000/forge-api/integrations/github/callback
# The same callback serves Continue with GitHub on /login and Connect
# GitHub on an application. Restart the API after changing these.
# FORGE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# FORGE_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Dashboard origin for the OAuth redirect (cookie lives here).
# FORGE_PUBLIC_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:3000
# URL GitHub POSTs webhooks to. Loopback and private IPs are not registered.
# Dashboard in front: https://your-public-host/forge-api
# API reached directly: https://your-public-host
# Restart the API, then save the application binding again.
# A tunnel is operator configuration. Forge does not start one.
# FORGE_WEBHOOK_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# Personal PaaS allowlist. Comma-separated numeric GitHub user ids
# (https://api.github.com/users/<login> field "id"). Empty refuses every
# GitHub login and GitHub connect. A webhook is still accepted only when
# its HMAC matches. Restart the API after changing this.
# FORGE_GITHUB_ALLOWED_USER_IDS=
# Zone Forge assigns as https://{slug}.{zone}/ . Leave empty on a laptop.
# Setting it makes the worker ask Let's Encrypt for those names, which
# fails closed (and can fail the Caddy reload) until DNS points here.
# FORGE_APPS_DOMAIN=
# Dashboard hostname Caddy publishes when FORGE_APPS_DOMAIN is set.
# GitHub webhooks and the OAuth callback use this origin.
# FORGE_CONTROL_HOST=
# FORGE_DASHBOARD_UPSTREAM=host.docker.internal:3000
